An undefined reference to `crc8_ccitt` indicates that the CRC library was not linked, which happens when `CONFIG_CRC` is not enabled. The Flash Circular Buffer (FCB) subsystem uses CRC8 for data integrity checks, but this can be disabled at runtime on a per-instance basis.

The file `subsys/fs/fcb/fcb_elem_info.c` contains the function `fcb_elem_crc8`, which calculates the CRC and calls `crc8_ccitt`. This function is compiled as part of the FCB module, but it should only be compiled with its CRC logic if `CONFIG_CRC` is enabled. Otherwise, it should provide a stub that returns an error, indicating that CRC functionality is not supported.

The fix is to wrap the implementation of `fcb_elem_crc8` with `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CRC)` preprocessor directives. When `CONFIG_CRC` is not enabled, the function will return `-ENOTSUP`, correctly signaling that the operation is not supported. This resolves the linker error by removing the reference to `crc8_ccitt` when the CRC library is not included in the build.

